-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the place read by a good point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ belongs to `A.nonunits`. Two function fields are in play: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$, and `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$, namely the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, and `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` denotes the resulting embedding.
--
--   Reduction data over the residue field. `W` is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A`, and `hW` says that its members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: those places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the geometric $j$-generator lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of invariants $j$ such that every elliptic curve with invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion affine point. `R₀` is a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` relative to $A$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with order functions, and compatibility with $A\to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ on constants. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that whenever a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ has its image under coefficientwise inclusion in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀`-residue is, as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Igusa components. $\zeta$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an element of `Idx q`), and `OIg` assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each point of the projective line over $\mathbb Z/q$. Four hypotheses constrain it: `hIg_inf` describes `OIg (lineInfty q)` as the Gauss ring attached to $A$, $f$ belonging to it exactly when $f\cdot y = x$ coefficientwise for Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction; `hIg` says every line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma)\cdot\mathrm{lineInfty}$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with `OIg ℓ` the preimage of `OIg (lineInfty q)` under the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says `OIg` is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the preimages of the `OIg ℓ` under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family.
--
--   Supersingular components. `OSS` assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each $s\in W$. `hSS_A` says that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `OSS s` exactly when it lies in $A$. `hSS_over` relates `OSS s` to $s$ through `R₀`: for $f\in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $j$ (the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb`) has non-negative order, and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OSS s`, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that `R₀`-residue the difference $f-a$ lies in `OSS s` and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix` says each `OSS s` is its own preimage under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr` provides, for each $s$, an element $t\in$ `OSS s` with $t-a$ a unit of `OSS s` for every $a\in A$.
--
--   The prolongation. `R` is a `RegularProlongation` of `fieldBar q M'` over $A$ with residue field `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`: a valuation subring `R.integers` inducing $A$ on constants, with surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with constants and with the normalisation property `exists_smul_mem`. The hypotheses `hR` and `hR₀O` state that `R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)` and that membership in `R₀.integers` is equivalent to membership of the image in `OIg (lineInfty q)`.
--
--   Arithmetic data. $\pi\in A$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$. Next, $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lies in $A$, with the hypotheses that $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, has algebraically closed residue field, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$. Further, $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (so $A_1=A\cap K_1$), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring. The field `fieldBar q M'` is given its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   The assertion is then the following. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying four conditions: (i) the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; (ii) $F_0$ is stable under every level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; (iii) for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, elements of the compositum $T(K')$ of $F_0$ with the image of $K'$ are linearly independent over the constants in the strong sense that a relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ with $a_i\in T(K')$ and $(c_i)$ a $K'$-linearly independent family in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ forces all $a_i=0$; (iv) $F_0$ contains every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent expansion has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of `coeffEmb`.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum over $k_0$ of $F_0$ and the image of $K_1$. Let $T_1$ carry an $A_1$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion, in the sense that the image of $a\in A_1$ in `fieldBar q M'` is the constant $a$. Let $j_1\in T_1$ be the element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the inclusion of the modular invariant $j$ (the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb`), assumed nonzero. Let `NIg` be a finite set of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to that field such that (a) for every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `R.integers` and its `R`-residue equals $j$ applied to its `R₀`-residue, and (b) a place $Q$ belongs to `NIg` exactly when there is $s\in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ is in the valuation subring of $Q$, for all $g$.
--
--   On the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) — the gluing (pushout) of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin`, the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$, and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf`, those integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$ and chart maps `ιFin`, `ιInf` — the following predicates are introduced. For $x\in\mathfrak X_1$ and $f\in T_1$: `InStalk x f` holds when for every point $y$ of either chart with image $x$ there are $g,h$ in the corresponding chart algebra with $h\notin y$ and $f\cdot h=g$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g\in y$. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and satisfies: the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$ (so $x$ is a closed point); for every point $y$ of the finite chart above $x$, every element of `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a nonunit of `R.integers` lies in $y$; the same for the infinite chart; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart above $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. For a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, `Reads x Q` holds when every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in `R.integers`, has `R`-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the `R`-residue is a nonunit there precisely when `InMax x f`. Finally `OffBranch x` holds when for every line $\ell\ne\mathrm{lineInfty}$ and every point $y$ of either chart above $x$ there is an element of the corresponding chart algebra whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a nonunit of `OIg ℓ` and which does not lie in $y$.
--
--   The conclusion is a single statement: for every $x\in\mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x`, and all places $Q,Q'$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` with `Reads x Q` and `Reads x Q'`, one has $Q=Q'$. The predicates `Centred` and `OffBranch`, although introduced among the local definitions, do not occur in this conclusion.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the correspondence between closed points of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of the level-$q^2M'$ modular function field and places of the Igusa reduced function field: a good point determines at most one place that it reads. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel), where the reading point is used to attach residue discs to the points of the semistable Igusa model.
